/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:179:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:180:Connect same-colored foreground components with one-cell-wide orthogonal paths around teal wall segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:182:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:183:- The dominant color is the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:184:- Teal cells are fixed wall segments and are never source connectors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:185:- Other foreground colors appear as one or more 4-connected components; colors with a single component stay unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:186:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:187:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:188:- For each non-background, non-teal color, read its 4-connected components in row-major order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:189:- Connect each consecutive pair by the shortest clear L-shaped path between the two components.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:190:- Clear paths may pass only through background or the same color, and they preserve the previous travel axis when both bends are possible.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:191:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:192:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:193:- The output is not a global recolor: each color traces a routed chain through its own components while teal cells and other colors act as blockers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:194:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:195:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:196:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:197:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="668eec9a" lines="29-47">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:198:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:199:Summarize the foreground line objects as ordered horizontal color stripes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:200:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:201:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:202:- A dominant background fills a rectangular grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:203:- Each non-background color forms one contiguous one-cell-thick line segment.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:204:- The line segments have distinct topmost rows, and there are at most five of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:205:  them.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:206:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:207:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:208:- Sort the foreground colors by the topmost row occupied by their line
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:209:  segment.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:210:- Create a 5x3 output filled with the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:211:- Place one solid 1x3 row for each foreground color, preserving that
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:212:  top-to-bottom order and padding any unused rows above with background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:213:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:214:Key insight: The exact line length and slope do not matter; only the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:215:vertical order of the colored line segments is encoded in the output stack.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:216:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:217:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:218:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:219:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="fc10701f" lines="20-35">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:220:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:221:Move the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:222:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:223:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:224:- The dominant background contains black obstacle segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:225:- There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:226:- The two rectangles share either their row span or their column span, so the move is straight and axis-aligned.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:227:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:228:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:229:- Erase the original orange rectangle to the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:230:- Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:231:- Between the two rectangles, paint red across the moving rectangle's width or height only at corridor cells flanked by black obstacle segments perpendicular to the movement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:232:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:233:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:234:- The black segments define gates in the straight corridor; only those gated openings, not every swept background cell, become red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:235:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:236:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:237:
