/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:239:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:240:Complete a grid of colored blocks to match a minimap legend in the top-left corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:241:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:242:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:243:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:244:- Top-left corner: a small sprite of single colored pixels forming a minimap pattern on a regular lattice.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:245:- Main area: uniformly colored square blocks (NxN) arranged on a regular grid; some positions are empty (bg).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:246:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:247:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:248:- The legend pixels define a color pattern; each pixel's lattice position maps to a block position in the main grid via a fixed scale factor and offset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:249:- Existing colored blocks confirm the scale/offset alignment.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:250:- For every legend pixel whose corresponding grid position is empty, place a new block of that color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:251:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:252:Key insight: The top-left pixel pattern is a scaled-down minimap of the block layout; the mapping is inferred from blocks already present.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:253:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:254:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:255:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:256:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="53fb4810" lines="105-119">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:257:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:258:Extend marker tiles outward from '+' shapes by repeating them to the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:259:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:260:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:261:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:262:- A dominant non-bg color forms several '+'-shaped objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:263:- Small colored patches (1–few cells) sit adjacent to each arm of a '+'.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:264:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:265:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:266:- For each marker tile touching a '+', determine which side of the '+' it sits on.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:267:- Project the tile away from the '+' in that direction, repeating the tile pattern periodically until the grid boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:268:- '+' pixels are never overwritten.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:269:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:270:Key insight: Each marker's attachment side determines its extension direction; the pattern repeats periodically, not as a single copy.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:271:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:272:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:273:
