/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:275:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:276:Redraw foreground objects as nested square rings ordered by object size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:277:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:278:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:279:- The grid has one dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:280:- Every foreground object is a 4-connected monochromatic component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:281:- Foreground object areas are distinct.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:283:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:284:- Sort the foreground objects by decreasing pixel count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:285:- Create a square output with side length 2 * number_of_objects - 1.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:286:- The largest object color fills the outer ring, each next object color fills
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:287:  the next inner ring, and the smallest object color fills the center pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:288:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:289:Key insight: The objects' original shapes do not get copied; their areas
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:290:determine only the outside-to-inside order of the nested square pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:291:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:292:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:293:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:294:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="train" puzzle_id="87ab05b8" lines="9-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:295:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:296:Erase all distractor pixels and expand the single red control pixel into the grid quadrant that contains it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:297:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:298:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:299:- The grid has one dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:300:- Exactly one red pixel is the control pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:301:- Other non-background pixels are distractors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:302:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:303:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:304:- Clear the canvas to the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:305:- Split the grid into equal top/bottom and left/right halves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:306:- Fill the quadrant containing the red control pixel with red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:307:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:308:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:309:- The red control pixel selects a whole half-grid quadrant by its row half and column half; all other foreground pixels are noise.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:310:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:311:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:312:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:313:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="train" puzzle_id="5ad8a7c0" lines="10-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:314:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:315:Connect the innermost mirrored marker pair(s) by filling their horizontal span.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:316:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:317:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:318:- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:319:- Each foreground row contains exactly two foreground pixels mirrored across the vertical center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:320:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:321:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:322:- Find the foreground row pair(s) with the smallest horizontal gap between the two markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:323:- Fill every pixel between those two markers in each selected row with the foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:324:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:325:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:326:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:327:- Wider marker pairs are context; the closest marker pair(s) show the unresolved horizontal segment.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:328:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:329:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:330:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:331:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="58f5dbd5" lines="20-34">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:332:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:333:Carve color-matched motifs into solid blocks and pack them into a compact grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:334:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:335:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:336:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:337:- Several solid 5×5 monochrome blocks, each a distinct non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:338:- For each block color, a small same-colored motif sprite elsewhere on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:339:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:340:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:341:- Match each motif to its same-colored 5×5 block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:342:- Center the motif within the block and recolor those cells to bg (punching holes).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:343:- Pack all carved blocks into an output grid preserving their original row/column order, separated by 1-cell gaps and a 1-cell outer border.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:344:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:345:Key insight: The motif acts as a stencil — it's not stamped onto the block but carved out of it as background holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:346:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:347:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:348:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:349:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="train" puzzle_id="25c199f5" lines="30-44">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:350:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:351:Pack the non-background rows from three separated panels into one panel, scanning panels right-to-left.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:352:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:353:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:354:- A rectangular grid contains three equal-size panels separated by two full-height divider columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:355:- The background is the dominant color; divider pixels use a color that appears only in the divider columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:356:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:357:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:358:- Read panels from right to left, and within each panel read rows from top to bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:359:- Keep each row that contains any non-background pixel, discarding all-background rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:360:- Place the kept rows at the bottom of a single panel-shaped output, padding above with background rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:362:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:363:- The task is row packing: the divider columns mark independent panels, and only the occupied rows are moved.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:364:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:365:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:366:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:367:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="train" puzzle_id="5adee1b2" lines="8-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:368:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:369:Use the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:370:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed174941624/6/prompt.md:371:Input structure:
